		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=9122&amp;sid=c2fe5f1ae2cca10913afe104dcbfa14f#9122"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Thu Jun 13, 2002 5:24 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=9122&amp;sid=c2fe5f1ae2cca10913afe104dcbfa14f"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Love.  Yeah, I know, <u>there’s</u> a new topic. As you know by now, that’s a word that both scares me and leaves me confused. Not that I ever noticed it before, but I realize I’ve armored and armed myself against it. And, like a good little Ranger should, I’ve studied it from afar. Tracked it through it’s habitat, watched it’s mannerisms and quirks. I’ve seen it sit idol as both weak and strong have passed by or stand silently by, offering support and courage. I’ve seen it spur people into actions beyond their capability, but I’ve also seen it leap onto its victim with the ferocity of a rabid werewolf and shred anything that gets in it’s path. Not that I consider Love to be my enemy. It’s a chaotic beast that can bring untold happiness or pain. I’ve just come to learn that pain is what it likes to bring me. I’ve laid down my own blood to defend someone or something that another loves. I‘ve even turned my blade and walked away from battle at the request of someone in love. Love however, is for other people. I cling tightly to those who are important to me but I’ve learned to not expect them to love me and, more importantly, not to love them back too much. Yet with all I’ve studied of it and all I’ve done to prepare myself for it, I still have failed to understand it. For the whole time I was tracking it and watching, It was tracking and watching me. It’s learned me well, better than I’ve learned myself. And now… Well, maybe I don’t understand it like I thought I did.
<br />

<br />
 
<br />
<i></i><br />_________________<br />Morani 
<br />
Wanderer of Tunare, 
<br />
Protector of The Mother's children.</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
			</tr>
