		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=9124&amp;sid=c2fe5f1ae2cca10913afe104dcbfa14f#9124"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Thu Jun 13, 2002 5:34 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=9124&amp;sid=c2fe5f1ae2cca10913afe104dcbfa14f"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp I don’t know how much I’m going to be writing for a while. I’ve resolved to not think as much and to feel more. Its definitely got its advantages lately and I’m a LOT more happy when I just feel. But, thinking is why I have these “ink chats”
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp When I start to think about it, I remember all the reasons I should not be doing this, all the promises sworn in to a pillow as a red eyed child, all the proud declarations of independence and lack of need. But when I don’t think, its like they’re at the other end of a long, hollow log. I can’t describe what it feels like when I’m not thinking. Its like what I always imagined what it would feel like to ride a horse as it runs free. Once you get past trusting the horse, its an amazing ride; thrilling, carefree, heart racing, overfilled with vitality. And this horse I <u>know</u> is not going to throw me. So, off I ride.
<br />

<br />
 
<br />
<i></i><br />_________________<br />Morani 
<br />
Wanderer of Tunare, 
<br />
Protector of The Mother's children.</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
