		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=9125&amp;sid=c2fe5f1ae2cca10913afe104dcbfa14f#9125"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Thu Jun 13, 2002 5:35 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=9125&amp;sid=c2fe5f1ae2cca10913afe104dcbfa14f"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">        I’m still stuck on why me and how could this have happened? I don’t know if I’ll ever understand the former. But the latter, well, Love cheated. I’m coming to accept it and honestly, I’m enjoying it. The last thing I ever expected Love to bring <u>me</u> was peace. I <u>like</u> thinking about the two of us. I <u>like</u> the idea of having a home together, having someone to come home to or being the person someone comes home to. I’m getting use to the idea of not being alone at night. Thinking about it makes me feel giddy and sure. I feel like I’m turning into a little girl again. Like Mother is giving me a chance to do it again, but to be happy this time.
<br />

<br />
That log is getting softer and I think the forest may just claim it yet.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
For the whole time I was tracking it and watching, It was tracking and watching me. It’s learned me well, better than I’ve learned myself. It disguised it’s self and waited until I could not defend against it, until it had me where it wanted me. Then it showed it’s self. In the last person I expected.
<br />

<br />
 
<br />
